# app.db used to be committed on purpose (a small, periodically-rebuilt
# snapshot). That stopped being safe once it started holding live,
# continuously-written, irreplaceable data with no other source of truth
# -- user accounts, Pick'em picks/settings, roster links -- that the
# running app itself mutates on every request. A tracked file that the
# app also writes to is a real data-loss risk: if a future commit ever
# touches its blob, `git pull` on a machine with real accumulated data
# either hard-fails (blocking every future pull until manually resolved)
# or, in the worst case, silently overwrites the live file with git's
# tracked version -- confirmed both failure modes in a throwaway test
# repo before making this change. See webapp/deploy/README.md's "Backups"
# section for the once-off migration steps this requires on any machine
# that already has app.db tracked, and for how it's actually kept safe
# now instead (an independent local backup rotation, since a database
# holding data this irreplaceable needs backups regardless of git).
data/app.db
data/backups/
data/analytics.duckdb
data/_dynastyprocess_data/
data/_nflverse_data/
data/_pokeapi_data/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
